t=\"Ἀπριλίων\" data-n=\"55\" data-lemma=\"Aprilis\">ΑΠΡΙΛΙΩΝ</span></span><span data-text=\"ζήσας\" data-n=\"60\" data-lemma=\"ζῶ\">ΖΗΣ</span><span data-text=\"ἔτη\" data-n=\"65\" data-lemma=\"ἔτος\">ΕΤΗ</span><span data-text=\"η\" data-n=\"70\" data-lemma=\"η\">Η</span><br id=\"al5-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">5</span><span data-text=\"μήνης\" data-n=\"75\" data-lemma=\"μείς\">ΜΗΝ</span><span data-text=\"ς\" data-n=\"80\" data-lemma=\"ς\">Σ</span><span data-text=\"κεῖτε\" data-n=\"85\" data-lemma=\"κεῖμαι\">ΚΕΙΤΕ</span><span data-text=\"μετὰ\" data-n=\"90\" data-lemma=\"μετά\">ΜΕΤΑ</span><br id=\"al6-diplomatic\"><span class=\"linenumber\">6</span><span data-text=\"τῆς\" data-n=\"95\" data-lemma=\"ὁ\">ΤΗΣ</span><span data-text=\"μάμης\" data-n=\"100\" data-lemma=\"μάμμη\">ΜΑΜΗ</span></span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div><div class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Dmitry Dundua, Robert Crellin</div><div id=\"edition-diplomatic-simple-lemmatized\"><div class=\"textpart\"><span class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\"><span data-text=\"Ἐνθάδε\" data-n=\"5\" data-lemma=\"ἐνθάδε\">ΕΝΘΑΔΕ</span><span data-text=\"κεῖτε\" data-n=\"10\" data-lemma=\"κεῖμαι\">ΚΕΙΤΕ</span><span data-text=\"Ἰεναρὶς\" data-n=\"15\" data-lemma=\"Ἰενάριος\">ΙΕΝΑΡΙΣ</span><span data-text=\"υἱὸς\" data-n=\"20\" data-lemma=\"υἱός\">ΥΙΟΣ</span><span data-text=\"Πρίμου\" data-n=\"25\" data-lemma=\"Πρῖμος\">ΠΡΙΜΟΥ</span><span data-text=\"τελευτᾆ\" data-n=\"30\" data-lemma=\"τελευτάω\">ΤΕΛΕΥΤΑ</span><span data-text=\"τᾖ\" data-n=\"35\" data-lemma=\"ὁ\">ΤΗ</span><span data-text=\"πρὸ\" data-n=\"40\" data-lemma=\"πρό\">ΠΡΟ</span><span data-text=\"θ\" data-n=\"45\" data-lemma=\"θ\">Θ</span><span data-text=\"καλανδῶν\" data-n=\"50\" data-lemma=\"Kalendae\">ΚΑΛΑΝΔΩΝ</span><span data-text=\"Άπριλίων\" data-n=\"55\" data-lemma=\"Aprilis\">ΑΠΡΙΛΙΩΝ</span><span data-text=\"ζήσας\" data-n=\"60\" data-lemma=\"ζῶ\">ΖΗΣΑΣ</span><span data-text=\"ἔτη\" data-n=\"65\" data-lemma=\"ἔτος\">ΕΤΗ</span><span data-text=\"η\" data-n=\"70\" data-lemma=\"η\">Η</span><span data-text=\"μήνης\" data-n=\"75\" data-lemma=\"μείς\">ΜΗΝΗΣ</span><span data-text=\"ς\" data-n=\"80\" data-lemma=\"ς\">Σ</span><span data-text=\"κεῖτε\" data-n=\"85\" data-lemma=\"κεῖμαι\">ΚΕΙΤΕ</span><span data-text=\"μετὰ\" data-n=\"90\" data-lemma=\"μετά\">ΜΕΤΑ</span><span data-text=\"τῆς\" data-n=\"95\" data-lemma=\"ὁ\">ΤΗΣ</span><span data-text=\"μάμης\" data-n=\"100\" data-lemma=\"μάμμη\">ΜΑΜΗΣ</span></span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "apparatus",
      "html": "<h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span class=\"lines 1-2\">lines.1-2: <span>Ἰε|νάρι(ο)ς Ferrua; Ἰε|ναρίς Libertini, Agnello</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 3\">line.3: <span>πρὸ θ´ καλ(ανδῶν) Agnello, Ferrua; πρὸ θ´ Libertini</span></span><br></li><li><span class=\"line 5\">line.5: <span>μήν(ης) ς´ Agnello; μνης ... Libertini</span></span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "translation",
      "html": "<h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo</a></p>  <p>Here lies Ienarios, son of Primos. He died nine days before the Kalends of April, having lived eight years and six months. He rests together with his mother.</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "translation",
      "html": "<h2>Italian translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\">Arianna Cinquatti</p>  <p>Qui giace Ienarios figlio di Priamos. Egli è morto 9 giorni prima delle Calende di Aprile, all'età di 8 anni e 6 mesi. Giace accanto a (sua) madre</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "commentary",
      "html": "<h2>commentary</h2>  <p>The funerary inscription for the young deceased Ienarios, son of Primos, follows Korhonen's (2004, 105) G8c pattern for Christian epitaphs, characterized by the formula <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">ἐνθάδε κεῖται</span>, the indication of the date of death by means of a finite verb, and the expression of the deceased's age through a participial construction. The deceased's name as engraved is presumably a variant for <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἰενάριος</span> (rather than <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἰεναρίς</span>, a feminine name, as suggested by Libertini and Agnello), in turn a variant of <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἰανουάριος</span> (other variants include <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἰανάριος</span> and <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἰανάρις</span>; for these variants in Sicily LGPN IIIA 215). His father bears the name <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Πρῖμος</span> (for the variant <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Πρεῖμος</span>, cf. IG XIV 498 = <a href=\"https://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic000648\" target=\"_blank\">ISic000648</a>). From ll. 5–6, <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">κεῖτε μετὰ | τῆς μάμη</span>, it may be inferred that the child was buried together with his mother. The term <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">μάμη</span> (a variant of <span class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">μάμμη</span>; cf. IG XIV 765a) lends an affectionate nuance to the statement and may be connected precisely with the young age of the deceased (cf. IMusCatania 204; see Korhonen 2004, 268).</p>  "
    },
    {
      "id": "bibliography",
      "html": "<h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Libertini 1931 44 no.7 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001870\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001870</a>  </li><li> Agnello 1953 no.61 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002211\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002211</a>  </li></ul>  <ul><li> Ferrua 1989 106 n. 407 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001995\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001995</a>  </li><li> Korhonen 2004 105, 268 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000028\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000028</a>  </li></ul>  "
    },
